# Conventional Commits — Metabolic

CI runs **PR Title Check** (`.github/workflows/pr-title.yml`). A PR fails if the title is not a Conventional Commit.

## PR titles (required)

Format: `type(optional-scope)!: description`

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `perf`, `build`, `ci`, `style`, `revert`

- Use `!` after the type/scope for breaking changes (`feat!: …` or `feat(api)!: …`)
- Description must follow `: ` (colon + space)

```text
✅ feat(exercise): weekly routine drag-assign and tempo schemes
✅ fix(sms): correct reminder timezone
✅ chore: bump dependencies
❌ Weekly routine drag-assign, day overrides, and tempo schemes
❌ Feat: add workouts
```

When creating a PR with `gh pr create`, always set `--title` to a valid Conventional Commit. If a title check fails, fix it with `gh pr edit <n> --title 'type(scope): …'`.

## Commit messages (preferred)

Prefer the same format for commit messages. Release-please uses Conventional Commits for changelog/version bumps; non-matching messages may be omitted from releases.
